<edge source="gulf_maritime_flashpoint::kinetic_strike_freq" target="energy_market_fragment::tanker_operational_avail" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.85</data>
  <data key="d36">A sustained rise in missile/armed-drone strikes increases insurer war-risk premiums and prompts shipowners and charterers to withdraw or reroute tankers away from the Gulf, directly reducing the proportion of tanker capacity available for commercial employment.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">gulf_maritime_flashpoint</data>
  <data key="d39">energy_market_fragment</data>
</edge>
<edge source="gulf_maritime_flashpoint::kinetic_strike_freq" target="energy_market_fragment::commodity_price_level_oi" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">An uptick in strikes in the Gulf region increases perceived supply risk and insurance/transportation costs, which feed directly into a higher crude oil risk premium and push benchmark prices up.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">gulf_maritime_flashpoint</data>
  <data key="d39">energy_market_fragment</data>
</edge>
<edge source="gulf_maritime_flashpoint::kinetic_strike_freq" target="financial_markets_stress::bond_yield_volatility" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.8</data>
  <data key="d36">A sudden rise in missile/rocket/armed‑drone strikes creates immediate tail‑risk repricing across sovereign and corporate debt, provoking rapid trading and hedging that raises observed and implied bond yield volatility.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">gulf_maritime_flashpoint</data>
  <data key="d39">financial_markets_stress</data>
</edge>
<edge source="gulf_maritime_flashpoint::kinetic_strike_freq" target="financial_markets_stress::market_liquidity_level" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">An uptick in kinetic strikes leads market‑makers and large liquidity providers to reduce inventory and widen quoted spreads in fixed‑income markets to limit exposure, lowering effective market liquidity and depth.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-3 months</data>
  <data key="d38">gulf_maritime_flashpoint</data>
  <data key="d39">financial_markets_stress</data>
</edge>
<edge source="gulf_maritime_flashpoint::kinetic_strike_freq" target="russia_ukraine_war::energy_trade_volumes" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.8</data>
  <data key="d36">Rising missile/drone strikes in the Gulf increase risk to tanker transits and prompt shipowners and charterers to suspend or divert shipments through the Strait of Hormuz, directly reducing cross-border diesel flows.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">gulf_maritime_flashpoint</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="gulf_maritime_flashpoint::kinetic_strike_freq" target="russia_ukraine_war::diesel_global_price" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">Higher strike frequency drives up war-risk insurance and voyage costs and forces longer reroutes, which raise delivered diesel costs and push up global diesel prices.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">gulf_maritime_flashpoint</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
