  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Rapid suspension of airline routes produces sudden sectoral shocks (airlines, insurers, energy, trade flows) that accelerate and amplify the transmission of fixed‑income shocks into equities, credit and commodity markets.</data>
