<edge source="energy_market_fragment::fuel_inventory_days_of_s" target="financial_markets_stress::market_risk_premia" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">A fall in days-of-supply tightens near-term fuel availability, increasing the perceived probability of demand disruption and amplifying required risk premia across credit and equity markets as investors price higher macro/earnings downside.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">energy_market_fragment</data>
  <data key="d39">financial_markets_stress</data>
</edge>
<edge source="energy_market_fragment::fuel_inventory_days_of_s" target="gulf_maritime_flashpoint::aviation_operational_cap" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.75</data>
  <data key="d36">Declines in refined fuel days-of-supply at Gulf terminals and airports force airlines to reduce flight frequencies, payloads, or cancel services due to refueling constraints and contingency fuel requirements, directly lowering civil aviation operational capacity.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">energy_market_fragment</data>
  <data key="d39">gulf_maritime_flashpoint</data>
</edge>
<edge source="energy_market_fragment::fuel_inventory_days_of_s" target="russia_ukraine_war::sanctions_enforce_streng" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Rapidly declining national or regional fuel stocks increases political pressure to secure imports, prompting governments to grant waivers or relax enforcement of diesel-related sanctions to avoid domestic shortages.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">energy_market_fragment</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="energy_market_fragment::fuel_inventory_days_of_s" target="us_china_rivalry::regulatory_scrutiny_leve" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.65</data>
  <data key="d36">A sharp decline in days-of-supply for refined fuels triggers emergency policy reviews that expand regulatory oversight of technologies linked to energy management and logistics, raising the intensity and scope of AI-related compliance checks and enforcement actions.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">energy_market_fragment</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_rivalry</data>
</edge>
<edge source="energy_market_fragment::commodity_price_level_oi" target="financial_markets_stress::sovereign_yield_level" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.85</data>
  <data key="d36">A sustained rise in crude oil benchmark prices lifts headline inflation and inflation expectations and forces markets to price earlier/tighter central bank action, which raises long-term sovereign yields.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">energy_market_fragment</data>
  <data key="d39">financial_markets_stress</data>
</edge>
<edge source="energy_market_fragment::commodity_price_level_oi" target="gulf_maritime_flashpoint::retaliation_pressure" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Sharp, sustained oil-price spikes tied to Gulf disruptions increase domestic economic pain and political pressure on governments to secure energy flows, thereby strengthening calls for military action or coercive measures to restore supplies.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">energy_market_fragment</data>
  <data key="d39">gulf_maritime_flashpoint</data>
</edge>
<edge source="energy_market_fragment::commodity_price_level_oi" target="us_china_rivalry::capital_flow_to_ai" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Sustained oil-price increases raise running costs for compute- and logistics-intensive AI firms and compress expected returns, prompting some institutional and VC investors to reallocate capital away from high-burn AI ventures toward energy, commodities, or defensive assets, reducing net capital flows into AI.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">energy_market_fragment</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_rivalry</data>
</edge>
