<edge source="financial_markets_stress::market_risk_premia" target="energy_market_fragment::fuel_inventory_days_of_s" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">Rising market risk premia increase the cost of financing inventory and collateral requirements for traders and refiners, prompting drawdowns of commercial fuel stocks and lowering days‑of‑supply held on hand.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">financial_markets_stress</data>
  <data key="d39">energy_market_fragment</data>
</edge>
<edge source="financial_markets_stress::market_risk_premia" target="russia_ukraine_war::sanctions_enforce_streng" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">Elevated market risk premia raise the cost and perceived legal/credit risk of cross‑border correspondent banking and commodity finance, prompting banks and insurers to tighten compliance and de‑risk, which functionally strengthens enforcement of diesel‑related sanctions against targeted counterparties.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">financial_markets_stress</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
