<edge source="financial_markets_stress::cross_asset_spillovers" target="energy_market_fragment::chokepoint_transit_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">Intensified cross‑asset spillovers lead banks to curtail trade finance and letters‑of‑credit issuance out of caution, which directly reduces the volume of financed shipments transiting major maritime chokepoints.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">financial_markets_stress</data>
  <data key="d39">energy_market_fragment</data>
</edge>
<edge source="financial_markets_stress::cross_asset_spillovers" target="gulf_maritime_flashpoint::route_suspension_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">Intense transmission of a fixed‑income shock into commodities, credit and insurance markets rapidly raises fuel costs and war‑risk/credit insurance premia and disrupts hedging, prompting airlines to suspend higher‑risk Gulf routes to avoid sudden cost and coverage gaps.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">financial_markets_stress</data>
  <data key="d39">gulf_maritime_flashpoint</data>
</edge>
<edge source="financial_markets_stress::cross_asset_spillovers" target="russia_ukraine_war::energy_trade_volumes" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">Stronger cross‑asset spillovers transmit fixed‑income shocks into commodity funding, freight and margining channels, producing margin calls and tighter short‑term credit that force traders to cut, delay or cancel diesel shipments, reducing cross‑border diesel trade volumes.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">financial_markets_stress</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
